<title>FRANCE: Rouen May grain exports more than triple year-ago.</title>
<headline>Rouen May grain exports more than triple year-ago.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from Rouen more than tripled to 593,480 tonnes in May 1997 from 174,000 tonnes in May 1996, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The May 1997 grain total included 421,136 tonnes of wheat and 172,344 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown by destination (in tonnes).</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    West Africa		   87,255</p>
<p>    Algeria			 22,700</p>
<p>    Cuba			    25,000</p>
<p>    Britain			 18,160</p>
<p>    Ireland			  4,615</p>
<p>    Italy			  211,386</p>
<p>    Morocco			 15,000</p>
<p>    Portugal			 3,300</p>
<p>    La Reunion island	    3,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			  30,720</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    South Africa		  24,800</p>
<p>    Saudi Arabia		  59,700</p>
<p>    Argentina		     25,000</p>
<p>    Greece			   3,000</p>
<p>    Iran			    26,494</p>
<p>    Italy			    2,350</p>
<p>    Tunisia			 25,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			   6,000</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
